@ [base_specification] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Field_Attention_Delineation_Latch_P0.sop

& [Problem] is open prose destabilizing a bounded tiny-model ABI
  + profile 0.1 and 0.2 completed transport but repeated a low-information filler through account and uncertainty fields
  + profile 0.3 proved that finite enums without array maxima can still create unbounded constrained generation
  + profile 0.4 proved that a strict attribution rule can turn an under-delineated observation into a transport-level fault

& [Decision] is typed selection followed by deterministic compilation
  + the model returns only finite semantic choices that influence the bounded P0 record
  + the host compiles exact self-bindings and a connected chain without choosing model relation kinds
  + open explanations are replaced by transparent compiler accounts
  + under-attributed non-coherence remains explicit whole-proposal tension and does not itself gain veto or admission authority

& [WhyNotFreeText] records the rejected alternative
  + more prompt wording did not remove repetition on the selected model
  + free text was not consumed by the host gate except as empty-versus-nonempty uncertainty
  + retaining it increased tokens and failure surface without adding replay authority

& [WhyNotHostInventedGraph] records the rejected alternative
  + a fully host-selected chain would demonstrate deterministic software rather than model-guided attention
  + typed ordering and relation kinds preserve a material model contribution
  + the host only supplies structurally necessary identity bindings accounts and adjacency projection

& [Limit] is mechanism validation only
  + connected structure does not prove relation-kind semantic correctness
  + four probes from one model are correlated observations
  + admitted_for_attention is not truth authorization safety or production trust
  + the v5 whole-proposal conflict followed by supported delineation is retained as a semantic-confidence warning

& [Conclusion] supports canonical amendment for P0
  = because: typed output reduced the public surface produced a replayable completion supported a no-latch control and still failed closed under a hostile boundary
